+Airbnb service fee
+Guest service fee
+The guest service fee can be found in the
+Price breakdown
+before
+booking a reservation
+.
+Guests pay a service fee ranging from 14.1% to 16.5% of the booking subtotal (the booking subtotal includes the nightly price and any additional fees charged by the host, but excludes the guest service fee and taxes). The guest service fee varies based on a variety of factors and may be higher or lower depending on the booking.
+For bookings where the guest pays using a different currency from the one set by the host for their listing, we adjust our fees to align with the value we provide our guests. For these cross-currency bookings, the guest service fee will include an additional amount, resulting in a guest service fee of up to 16.5% of the booking subtotal.
+2. Single fee
+With this structure, the entire fee is deducted from the host's payout. Most hosts pay 15.5%, remaining hosts typically pay 14%-16%, and hosts pay a 16% fee for listings in Brazil and Mexico.
+This fee structure is mandatory for most hosts, including traditional hospitality listings (e.g., hotels, serviced apartments, etc.),
+hosts who use property management software
+, and hosts in countries subject to this fee structure.
+VAT charges
+Depending on the laws of the jurisdiction involved,
+VAT
+may be applicable to the above fees. The service fee shown to hosts and guests is VAT inclusive, where applicable.
+We reserve the right to change our service fees at any time, and any changes will be made in accordance with our Terms of Service.
+Airbnb service fees for service and experience hosts
+For service reservations, we typically charge a 15% fee, with a minimum fee of $6 USD (or the local currency equivalent), which may vary based on the daily exchange rate. For experience reservations, we typically charge a 20% service fee.
